      {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/libuv/pulls/4",
        "id": 321953407,
        "node_id": "MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MzIxOTUzNDA3",
        "number": 4,
        "state": "closed",
        "locked": false,
        "title": "[android] Fix crash when starting a call on certain x86-64 devices",
        "user": {
          "login": "mikepavone",
          "id": 157731,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzczMQ==",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/mikepavone",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "body": "So at some point Google updated their seccomp profile for x86-64 to prevent the use of the epoll_wait syscall. When using bionic to call epoll_wait, this is not a problem as it instead uses epoll_pwait under the covers, but our old version of libuv is instead calling the syscall directly. Newer versions of libuv don't have this issue, but don't support Jelly Bean (thanks for the heads up on that Ben!) so patching this branch is the most expedient fix. Longer term we'll want to upgrade, but that's a bigger project than I intended to take on when looking into this bug.",
        "created_at": "2019-09-27T00:15:24Z",
        "updated_at": "2019-10-04T17:35:27Z",
        "closed_at": "2019-10-04T17:35:26Z",
