      {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/libuv/pulls/3",
        "id": 305260420,
        "node_id": "MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MzA1MjYwNDIw",
        "number": 3,
        "state": "closed",
        "locked": false,
        "title": "Netmap bindings for libuv",
        "user": {
          "login": "brian-armstrong-discord",
          "id": 25939803,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTM5ODAz",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/brian-armstrong-discord",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "body": "Netmap is a project that gives user-space networking to linux\r\napplications. Netmap binds to the network interface, and traffic\r\nsteering rules (generated by ethtool) drive packets into user-specific\r\nreceive queues. This completely bypasses the kernel except for NIC IRQs.\r\nBecause only some queues are controlled in userspace, the kernel\r\ncontinues to run other functionality like pings and ssh. In practice we\r\nfind this yields approximately 5x more efficient packet receives.\r\n\r\nhttps://blog.cloudflare.com/single-rx-queue-kernel-bypass-with-netmap/\r\n\r\nThis patch brings netmap to libuv for UDP packets. We connect the event\r\nloop to a single netmap queue. When the `use_netmap` flag is turned on\r\nfor new udp sockets, these sockets bypass the kernel calls and instead\r\noperate on top of the netmap rings.",
        "created_at": "2019-08-07T18:03:49Z",
        "updated_at": "2019-08-14T21:28:45Z",
        "closed_at": "2019-08-14T21:28:42Z",
        "merged_at": "2019-08-14T21:28:42Z",
        "merge_commit_sha": "2b664ffbf46422069c184026d89a497edcc8d1da",
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "requested_reviewers": [],
        "requested_teams": [],
        "labels": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "draft": false,
        "head": {
          "label": "discord:feature/netmap",
          "ref": "feature/netmap",
          "sha": "ac57107e50b8e6570db51a7fae4b35db54c0a813",
          "user": {
